===Etymology 2===
Likely from {{der|zh|sa|-}} or via {{der|zh|inc-mid|-}}. The ''{{w|Yiqiejing Yinyi (Huilin)|Yiqiejing Yinyi}}'' lists the form {{ltc-l|唄匿}}, likely related {{der|zh|sa-bhs|भाणक|t=chanter; speaker}}, from {{cog|sa|भणति}} and cognate with {{cog|pi|bhāṇaka|t=reciter of the scriptures}}; and also the more "orthodox" {{ltc-l|婆師}}, likely from {{m|sa|भाषते|t=to speak}}, compare {{cog|pgd|𐨧𐨮𐨡𐨁|t=speaks; to speak}}, {{cog|sa|भाषा|t=speech}}. In the Pali parallels, the verb for chanting or reciting a verse ({{m|pi|gāthā}}) is often the cognate {{m|pi|bhāsati}}.

Some older works suggest derivation from {{noncog|sa|पाठ}} (e.g. {{zh-ref|Soothill & Hodous, 1937}}), but with semantic and phonological difficulties.

