===Etymology 1===
Core meaning likely "empty, hollow" → "vast, boundless," derived from the resonant interior of the instrument {{och-l|庚}}. The sense "paved courtyard/temple path" represents an open linear passage between structures.

Perhaps related to {{och-l|途|road}} ({{zh-ref|Wang, 1982}}). {{zh-ref|Schuessler (2007)}} alternatively compares {{cog|aav-pro|*glɔːŋ}}, whence {{cog|mnw|ဂၠံၚ်}}, {{cog|kns|gəlɔŋ}}, {{cog|kdt|tr=khlù:aŋ}}.

The use of "唐" (Tang Dynasty) to mean "Chinese" is because the Tang Dynasty is viewed to Chinese people as one of the [[golden age]]s of their history.

